[17592186305873 1089 "q-119184" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305873 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534726 true] [17592186305873 1100 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-x?$" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305873 1113 #uuid "4db1550d-68e2-55f5-aa48-87d9e6b19e56" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305873 1145 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,2),(-2,-1)$ and $(2,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,2)}=1-(-2)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,-1)}=1-(-2)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=1-2=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/911af9ca268f5f4c9cbac7b9c063eae54defce6d99dfadef609892b93ad58ae4.png)" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305875 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305876 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305877 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305878 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305879 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1041 "selection" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305877 13194139534726 true] [17592186305874 1110 #uuid "61581a2f-1fda-56f8-9c23-70c80ebb3de3" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305875 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/3d6fc3c9462967aec890b1f681460a7b350b580c1b5bb55d37ccfe88c485eb36.png" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534726 true] [17592186305875 1111 #uuid "63195e44-9086-53e3-8574-d3726e38a6e8" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305876 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/d5e9f55d20c0b7fc515ea598d150017148342a6ba9082068823dd23c01e0eede.png" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534726 true] [17592186305876 1111 #uuid "e61ba0fc-2f96-5f0f-b47b-442ec325eaf2" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305877 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/911af9ca268f5f4c9cbac7b9c063eae54defce6d99dfadef609892b93ad58ae4.png" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305877 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534726 true] [17592186305877 1111 #uuid "e867f88d-aa0f-5c8f-8729-bd3fe8eb827c" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305878 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/467f0de9a886dbdb4d7620a4249379c2a8a661738960c3242d5e6618c35eb22b.png" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534726 true] [17592186305878 1111 #uuid "6f05679d-fa90-542d-ad09-708385c017f2" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305879 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/4d1215951efd9dbf2abcb8fe1c4a0856bbaa9bff70a3ae69c0da33bc2d157f82.png" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534726 true] [17592186305879 1111 #uuid "6ff053a3-6803-5b31-8710-0c1ce3ecdb9a" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305880 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305881 13194139534726 true] [17592186305880 1089 "q-119194" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305880 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534726 true] [17592186305880 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x+2$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point along the line $x=0,$ the slope field has a positive slope\n- At every point along the line $x=-1,$ the slope field is horizontal\n- At every point along the line $x=-2,$ the slope field has a positive slope" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305880 1113 #uuid "68b47d11-a021-5ca6-a752-6f99062a5a8b" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305880 1145 "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $x,$ the slope does not vary with $y.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Consider a point of the form $(0,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,y)}=2(0)+2=2>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(0,y)$ is positive for any $y.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(0,y)$ is equal to $2$ for any $y.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(-1,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,y)}=2(-1)+2=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(-1,y)$ is horizontal for any $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Consider a point of the form $(-2,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,y)}=2(-2)+2=-2<0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(-2,y)$ is negative for any $y.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(-2,y)$ is equal to $-2$ for any $y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/8d40c405f3f4db66a18e06a5327e86600081a6bc57b502ebed9c94471a0d5857.png)" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305882 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305883 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305884 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305885 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305886 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1041 "selection" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305885 13194139534726 true] [17592186305881 1110 #uuid "caff0cc2-5cb4-5a1d-b38a-39f62b81dabd" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305882 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305882 1111 #uuid "809a515f-2671-5f91-8153-b7defac35fb5" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305883 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305883 1111 #uuid "1e41064b-7938-5eb6-9d44-ac8cf9ba31dd" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305884 1034 "I only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305884 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305884 1111 #uuid "9405908b-b6ff-5be2-ad08-a3b44f98fd91" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305885 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305885 1111 #uuid "dd17f401-6e06-5f25-9880-098485c3d7c5" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305886 1034 "II only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305886 1111 #uuid "f1fd8d68-b69b-5f96-9008-5250e81518d6" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305887 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305888 13194139534726 true] [17592186305887 1089 "q-119206" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305887 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534726 true] [17592186305887 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}-3x$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point along the line $x=2,$  the slope field has a negative slope\n- At every point along the line $x=0,$  the slope field is horizontal\n- At every point along the line $y=1,$ the slope of the slope field does not vary" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305887 1113 #uuid "3abc9452-624e-5579-a29d-03f9a68262cf" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305887 1145 "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $x,$ the slope does not vary with $y.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Consider a point of the form $(2,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,y)}={2}^{2}-3(2)=-2,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(2,y)$ is negative for any $y.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(0,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,y)}={0}^{2}-3(0)=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(0,y)$ is horizontal for any $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,1)}={x}^{2}-3x,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(x,1)$ depends on $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"\n\nWe can use the information given by the true statements to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/e2ce8d7df3d0ceee4f8c9dcf368940006f1266a751c2f8e5ea8afdcfb90bf7ac.png)" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305889 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305890 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305891 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305892 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305893 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1041 "selection" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305892 13194139534726 true] [17592186305888 1110 #uuid "396d2c48-5f8f-52f5-b05c-513636b29ee3" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305889 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305889 1111 #uuid "01e55814-eeb5-5d67-a58f-013d0f4491bb" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305890 1034 "I only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305890 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305890 1111 #uuid "7d49ad34-cc6f-5ef1-8171-6756b4a13b8f" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305891 1034 "III only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305891 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305891 1111 #uuid "c18ea625-0115-5561-9143-cbe962a27cab" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305892 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305892 1111 #uuid "342e8986-e752-5c8c-98bf-c3447e6699fc" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305893 1034 "II only" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534726 true] [17592186305893 1111 #uuid "d32f2eca-0a06-5c68-8bc1-416688b63393" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305894 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305895 13194139534726 true] [17592186305894 1089 "q-119209" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305894 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534726 true] [17592186305894 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-{x}^{3}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point along the line $x=1,$  the slope field is horizontal\n- At every point along the line $x=0,$  the slope field has a positive slope\n- At every point along the line $y=2,$ the slope of the slope field varies" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305894 1113 #uuid "f3ead8fb-34d4-5aea-a509-a80a04973d86" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305894 1145 "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $x,$ the slope does not vary with $y.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Consider a point of the form $(1,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,y)}=1-{1}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(1,y)$ is horizontal for any $y.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Consider a point of the form $(0,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,y)}=1-{0}^{3}=1>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(0,y)$ is positive for any $y.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(0,y)$ is equal to $1$ for any $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,2)}=1-{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(x,2)$ depends on $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"\n\nWe can use the information given by the true statements to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/85d8f71c4680a56d5722b87fa5f7b2a7623fd2457f540c2cd15cd3bfa29694f3.png)" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305896 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305897 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305898 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305899 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305900 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1041 "selection" 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305896 13194139534726 true] [17592186305895 1110 #uuid "8640bf9a-f040-5c14-b49b-51693fcc0301" 1319